  "notes": "{継|つ}ぐ means to succeed or take over something from a predecessor.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{家業|かぎょう}→家業：12353_kagyou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{継|つ}ぐ: to take over the family business\n- ⟦{後|あと}→後：09580_ato⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{継|つ}ぐ: to succeed someone\n- ⟦{跡|あと}→跡：02174_ato⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{継|つ}ぐ: to inherit a position/legacy\n- ⟦{王位|おうい}→王位：13586_oui⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{継|つ}ぐ: to succeed to the throne\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {継|つ}ぐ: to succeed, inherit\n- ⟦{注|つ}ぐ→注ぐ：02470_tsugu⟧: to pour (liquid)\n- ⟦{接|つ}ぐ→接ぐ：02471_tsugu⟧: to join, graft, splice\n- ⟦{次|つ}ぐ→次ぐ：02076_tsugu⟧: to rank next to\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{後継者|こうけいしゃ}→後継者：12592_koukeisha⟧: successor\n- ⟦{継承|けいしょう}→継承：13841_keishou⟧: succession, inheritance\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {継|つ}いでいる: has taken over / has inherited (resultative state)\n- Note: {継|つ}ぐ is punctual — it refers to the moment of succession or inheritance. {継|つ}いでいる describes the resulting state: the person now runs the business, holds the position, or carries on the tradition. ⟦{息子|むすこ}→息子：00799_musuko⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧⟦{店|みせ}→店：00497_mise⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{継|つ}いでいる means \"the son has taken over the shop (and now runs it),\" not \"is in the process of taking over.\"",
